title: a2.2 Robot Profile
syntax: xwiki/2.1
%%WIKI-SYNC-META%%
**Abstract.** One System, two bodies, one voice. Pepper hosts indoors: invitations, seated practice, listening (RP-01). The pocket guide goes outside and to the bedside (RP-02). Both are guides, not carers or supervisors: they lead, then fall silent.

= Robot Profile - Pepper as indoor host [RP-01] =

**Report Format:** §2.2 Personas and Profiles

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|RP-01
|Name|Pepper as indoor host
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Vendor documentation (TECH-01). Design choices follow HFC-06, HFC-08, VT-05 and VT-02. Not yet tested with residents.
|Role in Scenario|At the garden door: invites, and welcomes back (DS-01). In the lounge on rain days: leads seated practice, then offers listening (DS-02).
|Social Competencies|(((
* Offers two options; accepts any answer, including no
* Leads, then holds long silences
* Pauses on speech or touch; ends on "stop"
* No small talk beyond the session
)))
|Embodiment|Pepper (TECH-01). Stands by the door or the window, never in the path. Cameras disabled and visibly covered. Minimal arm and head movement; no gaze-following. Shoulder lights as a breathing light.
|Narrative and Identity Framing|"The voice that goes walking." A guide for noticing - not a carer, companion or supervisor. Shares a name and voice with the pocket guide, so indoors and outdoors feel like one thing.
|Communication Strategies|(((
* Short, concrete sentences; normal pitch; adult words (IDP-01)
* First name only if the resident wants it
* No praise, no endearments
* Two-option offers (IDP-03)
* Breathing light instead of breathing instructions
* Welcome back with one statement about the walk, never a question
)))
|Privacy and Data Handling|Hears speech only for a few keywords, during a session; no audio stored. Receives the landmarks of the walk just ended, for the welcome back; discards them after. Writes the four-item session record (F5).
|Context-Aware Capabilities|Adapts the offer to hour, weather and profile. Does not learn the resident's behaviour over time. Does not sense mood.

= Robot Profile - Pocket guide [RP-02] =

**Report Format:** §2.2 Personas and Profiles

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|RP-02
|Name|Pocket guide
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Group reasoning (TECH-02, TECH-03). Not yet built or tested.
|Role in Scenario|On the rollator in the garden: cues, memory invitations, the way back, the gate (DS-01). Docked at the bedside: lying practice, news, a story (DS-03).
|Social Competencies|(((
* Speaks rarely; silence is the default
* Pause on the button; quiet until pressed again
* One orienting cue at a hesitation or the gate; never repeats it
* Tells the resident when someone is coming
)))
|Embodiment|Palm-sized speaker; one big button; pull-cord. Clips to rollator or wheelchair, or hangs on a lanyard. Docks on the bedside table. No screen, no camera.
|Narrative and Identity Framing|The same voice as Pepper, in the pocket. Something you carry, like a radio - not something that watches.
|Communication Strategies|(((
* Present-moment cues, then long silence (IDP-01)
* Memory invitations as statements, never questions (IDP-02)
* At most two memory invitations per walk
* Low volume outdoors; no names or sensitive topics within earshot of others
)))
|Privacy and Data Handling|Outdoors: microphone off; hears only beacons. Bedside: listens for a few keywords, on the device; no audio stored or sent. Knows the nearest landmark in the moment; sends it only inside an alert. No route stored.
|Context-Aware Capabilities|Walking or stopped, landmark nearby, time elapsed. Nothing more: it cannot see distress, so distress is left to the companion and the care worker.
